      'Rule example: Assemble a 5-card hand of the same suit that totals exactly or as close to 51 as possible.',
      "Turn-flow example: Each turn (clockwise), a player MUST perform one of the following exchanges with the table:\n1. 1-for-1: Swap one card from your hand for one card from the table.\n2. 5-for-5: Swap your entire hand for all five cards on the table.\n3. Stop: If you have a high score (usually 40+), you may say 'Stop'. This triggers the final round.",
      'Scoring example: Collect 5 cards of same suit totaling as close to 51 as possible. Ace=11, K/Q/J=10, 2-10=face value. Exact 51 = instant win. Highest single-suit total when game stops (max 51). Exact 51 = instant win..',
